1. Student Identification
The studett scans an RFID card.
The ESP32 reads the UID and maps it to the corresponding student information.
2. Classroom Detection

ESP8266 nodes are installed as classroom/location nodes.

The ESP32 periodically communicates with the nodes to determine the
current classroom/location.

3. GPS

The prototype uses the smartphone as the GPS source.

The smartphone obtains its GPS coordinates and sends them to the ESP32
through Wi-Fi.

The ESP32 provides an HTTP endpoint:

/location

Example:

/location?lat=17.385044&lon=78.4866712. Classroom Detection

